1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,738
BRAMBLE: Case open!

2
00:00:01,738 --> 00:00:04,916
OTTO: Oh no! Mud on Mabel's new sign!

3
00:00:05,116 --> 00:00:08,052
IVY: Now we can't read the name.

4
00:00:08,452 --> 00:00:12,387
Today's case: the name on a muddy sign.

5
00:00:12,687 --> 00:00:16,706
A digraph means two letters, one sound.

6
00:00:17,106 --> 00:00:21,548
S and h say sh. Like fish.

7
00:00:21,948 --> 00:00:25,626
C and h say ch. Like chips.

8
00:00:26,226 --> 00:00:29,165
Pip wipes the mud away.

9
00:00:29,565 --> 00:00:33,083
OTTO: S. H. O. P. Suh-huh-op!

10
00:00:33,483 --> 00:00:35,903
IVY: Hmm. That's not a word.

11
00:00:36,303 --> 00:00:38,942
BRAMBLE: Let's not guess. Let's test.

12
00:00:39,342 --> 00:00:42,513
BRAMBLE: Can you show me the sh sound?

13
00:00:46,113 --> 00:00:48,761
BRAMBLE: What does the sign say?

14
00:00:49,161 --> 00:00:52,054
A. Suh-huh-op.

15
00:00:52,254 --> 00:00:54,381
B. Shop.

16
00:00:54,581 --> 00:00:56,525
Pause and think.

17
00:01:01,125 --> 00:01:04,235
Two letters can make one sound.

18
00:01:04,635 --> 00:01:07,401
S and h make sh.

19
00:01:07,801 --> 00:01:09,968
Sh. Op.

20
00:01:10,568 --> 00:01:11,624
Shop!

21
00:01:12,024 --> 00:01:14,042
It's B! Shop.

22
00:01:14,242 --> 00:01:16,862
OTTO: Oh! It says Mabel's Shop!

23
00:01:17,262 --> 00:01:20,707
BRAMBLE: Let's check another way. Count the sounds.

24
00:01:21,107 --> 00:01:24,682
Sh is one sound. One line.

25
00:01:25,082 --> 00:01:28,390
O and p. Two dots.

26
00:01:28,790 --> 00:01:31,847
Four letters. Three sounds.

27
00:01:32,247 --> 00:01:34,285
IVY: Three sounds make shop!

28
00:01:34,685 --> 00:01:36,035
BRAMBLE: Case solved!

29
00:01:37,535 --> 00:01:39,522
IVY: Now try ch, Otto.

30
00:01:39,922 --> 00:01:43,465
OTTO: Ch, ch, ch! I sound like a train!

31
00:01:44,065 --> 00:01:47,937
Remember. Two letters can make one sound.

32
00:01:48,437 --> 00:01:53,344
Say it with me. Two letters can make one sound.

33
00:01:55,144 --> 00:01:59,125
Try it at home. Hunt for sh words.

34
00:01:59,625 --> 00:02:03,362
Next case: the till that won't balance.

